uring introduced by Soviet leader Mikhail Gorbachev in the 1980s?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Perestroika, meaning restructuring, began in 1986 alongside glasnost (openness) and contributed to the Soviet Union\'s collapse.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-75de-9bf8-875cb61c5440","description":"Perestroika","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-7316-8e91-bafa49c40942","description":"Apparatchik","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-72b0-91db-f992908a5413","description":"Uskoreniye","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-7e99-8d35-bc84a6034831","description":"Khozraschyot","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-7dcc-a2ad-8cb6a586924f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Where did the battle of Waterloo take place?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Waterloo is in Belgium today, though the area was part of the United Kingdom of the Netherlands when the battle was fought in 1815.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-7bdc-9ef4-45c5d7fe99a5","description":"Belgium","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-75a7-a2c2-2c5cb25e9c2d","description":"France","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-7399-9b5c-3db5ea294ee1","description":"England","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-7468-939a-21252206e76e","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-7b5a-b04e-f57afa044fe3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which ancient people carved the rose-red city of Petra?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Nabataeans made Petra the center of their kingdom and engineered channels and cisterns to manage scarce water in the desert.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-7c13-a866-bebd46df8f93","description":"Nabataeans","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-7be5-80f8-35870af49435","description":"Phoenicians","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fb-77d8-b1cb-9f3ca1190221","description":"Babylonians","correct_answer":false},{"i