est in 1952 before reaching the summit in 1953?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Tenzing Norgay and Edmund Hillary reached the summit on May 29, 1953, and their ascent was celebrated as a joint achievement.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-7588-b3f2-308e6ea83135","description":"Tenzing Norgay","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-75ba-aab1-9b498a374a7a","description":"Sir Edmund Hillary","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-75e2-9879-e5ddd0c14cf8","description":"George Mallory","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-7d0f-8701-3c0b41a03930","description":"Reinhold Messner","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-727e-901c-9bafb8bc91f0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"From 1795-1806, which country was briefly known as the Batavian Republic?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Netherlands\' Batavian Republic was a French-backed successor to the Dutch Republic; in 1806, Napoleon replaced it with the Kingdom of Holland.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-7a72-86c9-6b50857cd180","description":"The Netherlands","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-7f19-bd43-bdd2c53f7bee","description":"Poland","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-7ba4-bb0f-5c54e1c459cd","description":"Portugal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-76c4-98e2-4b900e0fe787","description":"Greece","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-7a12-9c91-1408701e2060","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the Gulf War begin?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Gulf War began in 1990 after Iraq invaded Kuwait; the U.S.-led coalition launched Operation Desert Storm the following January.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-7cdb-9efe-1c4a16267c01","description":"1990","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-7569-b982-1bc8ed9bb411","description":"1983","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36fc-757b-ad82-9c651953b59a","description":"1971","correct_a